>> title: Shrimp and Soft Egg Rice
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: shrimp, eggs, rice, hong kong, stovetop, quick
>> counters: Cha Chaan Teng
>> aka: waat daan ha yan faan, 滑蛋蝦仁飯, 滑蛋, shrimp and egg over rice, soft scrambled egg with shrimp, sliding egg rice, prawn and egg rice
>> servings: 2
>> time: 25 min
>> slack: narrow — the egg comes off the heat while it still looks underdone, because it keeps setting in the pan; scrambled until it looks right it is curds, and curds are a different dish
>> step.1: toss and rest 10 min
>> step.2: beat it smooth, no streaks
>> step.3: fry 2 min, just pink through
>> step.4: egg over, lowest heat, off wet at 2 min

Toss @raw shrimp{10%oz}(285 g; peeled and dried on a towel) with @Shaoxing wine{2%tsp} and @white pepper{1/4%tsp}, and leave them to ~rest{10%min}.

Beat @eggs{5%large} with @evaporated milk{3%Tbs}, @cornstarch{1%tsp} and @kosher salt{3/4%tsp} until there are no streaks left.

Fry @&(~2)shrimp{} in @neutral oil{1%Tbs} in a #nonstick pan{} for ~fry{2%min}, until they are just pink through.

Pour @&(~2)egg{} over @&(~1)shrimp{} on the lowest heat the burner will hold, drag it in slow folds for ~fold{2%min}, slide it off while it is still wet onto @steamed jasmine rice{3%cups}(450 g), and scatter @scallion{1}(thinly sliced) over.
